Build a Salon Profile feature for a salon management dashboard with the following requirements:

1. Data Model

Create a SalonProfile entity with these fields:

salonId (unique identifier)
salonName (string, required)
address (string, required)
phoneNumber (string, required, validated format)
manager (object: managerId, managerName, managerEmail, managerPhone)
vision (text/long string — the salon's mission/vision statement)
photoUrl (string — relative path to stored image, nullable)
photoUpdatedAt (timestamp, optional)
createdAt, updatedAt (timestamps)
2. Permissions / Role-Based Access
View: any authenticated role tied to the salon (staff, manager, super admin) can view the full profile.
Edit: only manager and super_admin roles can update phoneNumber, address, vision, and photoUrl.
salonName and manager details are read-only in this module (or editable only by super_admin — confirm this choice explicitly in implementation).
Reject unauthorized edit/upload requests with a clear 403 error and message.
3. API Endpoints
GET /api/salons/:salonId/profile — fetch salon profile data
PATCH /api/salons/:salonId/profile — update editable fields only (phone, address, vision), with role-check middleware
POST /api/salons/:salonId/photo — multipart/form-data upload, saves file locally, returns new photoUrl
DELETE /api/salons/:salonId/photo — deletes file from disk, clears photoUrl, reverts to default placeholder
Return proper status codes (200, 400, 403, 404, 500) with a consistent error response shape
4. Salon Profile Photo — Local Storage
Store uploaded images on the server's disk under /uploads/salons/:salonId/profile.<ext>
Save only the relative path (e.g., /uploads/salons/123/profile.jpg) in the photoUrl field
Serve images via a static file route (e.g., Express app.use('/uploads', express.static('uploads')))
⚠️ Caveat: local storage only persists reliably on an always-on server with persistent disk (VPS, dedicated server, or Docker with a mounted volume). On platforms with ephemeral filesystems (Vercel, Heroku, Railway, etc.), uploaded photos will be lost on every redeploy/restart. Flag this to the team now; migrating to cloud storage later is straightforward if needed.

File handling:

Use multer (Node/Express) for multipart/form-data uploads
Validate file type (.jpg, .jpeg, .png, .webp) and size (max 5MB)
Resize/compress with sharp to a standard size (e.g., 500x500) before saving to disk
Delete the old photo file when a new one is uploaded (avoid orphaned files)
Auto-create the salon's upload folder if it doesn't exist (fs.mkdirSync with { recursive: true })
Show a static default avatar (e.g., /public/default-salon.png) when photoUrl is null
5. Frontend Behavior
Fetch profile data on dashboard load with a loading state and error/retry handling (skeleton or spinner, non-blocking)
Display all fields in a clean profile card/section, including the photo
Authorized roles (manager, super_admin):
Editable inputs (or an "Edit" toggle) for phone, address, and vision, with client-side validation before submit
Hover/tap overlay icon on the photo to trigger upload (file picker)
Client-side validation of file type/size before upload, with image preview before confirming
Upload progress indicator for larger files
Other roles: all fields, including photo, shown as read-only (no edit controls rendered)
Show success/error toast on save or upload
Update UI immediately after successful save/upload (avoid full page reload)
Graceful handling of upload failures (retry option, clear error message)
6. Data Handling / Storage
Store profile data in the backend database (MongoDB) with proper indexing on salonId
Validate and sanitize all input on both client and server side
Ensure PATCH updates only touch permitted fields (no mass-assignment vulnerabilities)